    <statement><p>Use <m>\cos(t)</m> and <m>\sin(t)</m>, with positive coefficients, to parametrize the intersection of the surfaces <m>x^2+y^2=49</m> and <m>z=8 x^{3}</m>.</p>
<p><m>\bf r\it (t)=\left\lt  \right.</m>
  <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/>,
  <fillin characters="20" name="MuLtIaNsWeR_AnSwEr0001_1"/>,
  <fillin characters="20" name="MuLtIaNsWeR_AnSwEr0001_2"/>
<m>\left. \right&gt;</m></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>7\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right);\,7\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right);\,8\mathopen{}\left(7\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right)\right)^{3}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>x^2+y^2=49</m> and on <m>z=8 x^{3}</m> can be written in the form: 


<m>x^2+y^2=49 \rightarrow \left(7 \cos t, 7 \sin t, z\right)</m> 


<m>z=8 x^{3} \rightarrow \left(x,y,8 x^{3} \right)</m> 


The points <m>(x,y,z)</m> on the intersection curve must satisfy the following equations:



<m>x=7\cos t</m>


<m>y=7\sin t</m> 


<m>z=8 x^{3}=8 (7 \cos t)^{3}</m> 


We obtain the vector parametrization: 


<m>\bf r\it (t)=\left\lt  7 \cos t, 7 \sin t, 8(7 \cos t)^{3} \right&gt;</m>





</solution>
